  "name": "03 — Identity: Brand",
  "text": "Locked. Competitive research confirmed this sits exactly where the\npremium end of the category sits — Athena and Persona both run a display serif over\na clean sans on a heritage palette.\n\n### Typography\n\nDisplay\n\nMarcellus — high-contrast Didot-style serif. Headlines, wordmark,\nfigures, section headings.\n\nBody\n\nTenor Sans — body copy, buttons, labels, interface.\n\nScript\n\nWindSong Medium — the tagline only, set large enough to stay readable.\n\nRejected across an extended\nexploration and not to be revisited: Bodoni Moda (twice), Hanken Grotesk, Italiana,\nJulius Sans One, Prata, DM Serif, Montserrat, Cormorant, Cinzel, Playfair, EB\nGaramond, Fraunces, Gilda, Instrument Serif, Libre Caslon, Pinyon Script, Great\nVibes, Petit Formal.\n\n### Palette\n\nFern#35443A\n\nInk#22302A\n\nCream#F3EFE6\n\nPaper#FAF8F2\n\nPale#B0C4B2\n\nMist#DDE5DC\n\nLight greens, creams, white and\nneutrals. The ink-and-brass direction was considered and rejected.\n\n### Logo\n\n- Primary — wordmark with ruled descriptor, Didot all-caps, wide\nletterspacing. Cream on deep fern with pale green rules.\n\n- White version — white wordmark with “Executive Staffing” set\nunderneath.\n\n- The accent on the È is always the same colour as the wordmark, never a\nseparate accent colour.\n\n- No standalone È letter mark. Rejected — it reads as odd on its own.\n\n- Relève Careers — same system, “CAREERS” as the ruled\ndescriptor. Cream-on-fern, fern, and white versions, plus a square avatar.\n\n### Business card\n\nFront — fern lockup on cream, “Consider it handled.” in WindSong,\nthen VIRTUAL EXECUTIVE ASSISTANTS · REMOTE TEAMS. Back — fern\nground, a QR code to the site as the focal point, kicker line\nFully Sourced · Continuously Managed · 30% of the Cost, thin hairline\ndivider, then the domain and phone. Company only — no name, no title."
