  "text": "Two accounts, two audiences, deliberately separate. One sells the\nservice; one recruits the people who deliver it.\n\n### @relevestaffing\n\nAudience: founders and business owners who need help and have not\nhired offshore before.\n\nJob: build trust. Answer the two real hesitations: can I trust this\nperson to handle it, and will they add work instead of removing it. Content pillars:\nhow we vet (the six fronts), what “handled” looks like week to week, the\nright-resume-wrong-fit story, and the Client and Talent Success Managers at work.\nNever cost-led hooks.\n\nBio: “Consider it handled. /\nVirtual executive staff, vetted on six fronts and fully managed. / Book a discovery\ncall ↓” → relevestaffing.com\n\n### @relevecareers\n\nAudience: offshore talent looking for real careers with real\nexecutives.\n\nJob: attract the calibre the promise depends on. Tagline\n“Take the watch.” — but always paired with a plain explanation of\nwhat Relève Careers actually is.\n\nOwn logo lockup in the same\nsystem: RELÈVE with CAREERS as the ruled descriptor, plus a square avatar.\n\n### Channels in use\n\nInstagram — @relevestaffingPrimary. Linked from the site footer.\n\nInstagram — @relevecareersTalent-facing. Exists; the footer points at the main account.\n\nFacebookPage 61593520618684.\n\nLinkedIn/company/relèveexecutivestaffing. Founder-role copy written for Sage.\n\nPosting planRequested for both accounts. Content style reference for careers: The Grapevine Agency (@grapevineagency) — bespoke corporate and domestic staffing, LA and NY.\nTo build\n\nEvery piece must say the staff are virtual. “Executive\nStaffing” reads as local placement unless the post says otherwise."
