  "text": "Every platform running Relève, what it does, and what it costs. The\nstanding rule is that nothing new gets added if it charges.\n\n### What you pay for\n\nGoogle Workspacehello@relevestaffing.com and its aliases (careers@, sjackson@, team@). Also the SMTP that sends every transactional email, via an app password — Google stopped accepting plain passwords in 2025.\nPaid\n\nNetlifyHosts both sites as separate projects: the app and the marketing site. Environment variables live here — including every secret. From 11 September it also runs the three scheduled jobs (Friday nudge, monthly pulse, monthly run) as scheduled functions in netlify/functions/, which call the app's own /api/cron/* routes with CRON_SECRET.\nPaid\n\nZoomMeeting links for interviews and screening calls, via server-to-server OAuth. Connected 18 September 2026.\nPaid, connected\n\nStripePercentage per transaction, no monthly fee. Live account connected 20 September 2026 — bank debit and card both on, deposits and retainer autopay running for real.\nPaid, connected\n\nSquarespace Domainsrelevestaffing.com, bought 17 Aug 2026. DNS lives here — the app is a CNAME from app to the Netlify site.\nPaid\n\nClaudeWhere the app is built and maintained.\nPaid\n\n### What is free\n\nThe email list: subscribers (PART 53, 29 October 2026)One list of every business owner who has given Relève an email, for the biweekly emails. Talent are never on it. Triggers copy in every new lead from prospects (website form, /discovery, /training, Calendly, console) and every executive from profiles; the backfill added everyone already there. Columns include origin (training, lead, client, import), source, subscribed, training_at and an unsubscribe_token. Training signups are filed as nurturing with a follow-up three days out. View subscriber_list for exports. File supabase/part53-subscribers.sql, applied to production 29 October 2026 and tested with a rolled-back signup. An export is at ~/Releve/releve-email-list.csv (7 contacts on day one, including Sage's own test client account and Nikka of Via Connect). Still to decide: which tool sends the biweekly email. Unsubscribe link, live 29 October 6:20 PM (shipped inside the other chat’s app deploy; verified: the page renders and an unknown token returns “That link is not active.”): a public page, /unsubscribe?t=TOKEN, where one press takes that address off the list (with a “Keep me on the list” undo), and POST /api/unsubscribe, which also answers mail apps’ one-tap Unsubscribe button (RFC 8058). Opening the link alone never unsubscribes anyone, because inbox link-scanners open every link. It sets subscribed = false and unsubscribed_at by the row’s unsubscribe_token. Whatever sends the biweekly email must put unsubscribeUrl(token) in every footer and listUnsubscribeHeaders(token) in the headers, and must skip anyone with subscribed = false (lib/subscribers.ts). Files: lib/subscribers.ts, app/unsubscribe/page.tsx, components/UnsubscribeForm.tsx, app/api/unsubscribe/route.ts; typecheck clean, committed.\n\nResendEvery transactional email, and Supabase Auth's sign-in links. Free tier, 3,000 a month. Host smtp.resend.com, username the literal word resend, password the API key. Domain verified with DKIM, two sending CNAMEs and DMARC.\nFree\n\nSupabaseThe database, sign-in, and file storage for photos and verification documents. Free tier — which means no backups, hence the local backup script.\nFree\n\nGoogle CloudProject releve-507223, under the relevestaffing.com organization. Holds the OAuth client behind Google sign-in and, once switched on, Calendar.\nFree\n\nCalendlyDiscovery-call booking from the website. Separate from the app's own interview scheduling, which does not use it.\nFree\n\nGitVersion history, on the Mac only. A private GitHub repo would make it off-machine and costs nothing.\nLocal only\n\n### How it fits together\n\nDomain → sites\n\nSquarespace holds DNS. relevestaffing.com points at the marketing site;\na CNAME on app points at the Netlify app project. Both have their own\nHTTPS certificate.\n\nSign-in\n\nSupabase Auth, two ways in: a magic link by email, or Google — which runs\nthrough the OAuth client in Google Cloud. Both land on the same callback.\n\nEmail out\n\nThe app sends through Google Workspace SMTP rather than a third-party service,\nso mail comes from Relève rather than a vendor. Ten templated events:\ninvitations, application received and a new application (both on an\napply), invited to the assessment, candidate ready (sent to the executive the moment a release is\napproved), interview booked, candidate approved by the executive, offer made,\nvetting verified or rejected, new message, the Friday nudge, and a flagged\ncheck-in. None of this has been verified to arrive — see Still open. The\nintended fix is Resend, free to 3,000 messages a month, which is both the app's\nSMTP and Supabase's, so sign-in links stop coming from Supabase.\n\nFiles\n\nThree Supabase buckets, all private: avatars, vetting and\nintros (talent introduction videos, added 10 September). Nothing is\nreachable by URL — the app mints a link that expires in a minute after checking\nwho is asking.\n\nScheduled tasks\n\nThree, all guarded by the same CRON_SECRET and all running with\nthe service role because they must see every placement: checkin-nudge\n(Friday, to talent), monthly-billing, and pulse-nudge (first\nworking day, to executives — added 6 September).\n\nScheduling\n\nAvailability windows are set in the app. Google Calendar, when connected,\nsubtracts genuinely busy time using free/busy only. Zoom would issue the\nmeeting link.\n\nDeploys\n\nNo repository is connected to Netlify, so deploys happen only from Terminal.\nThe build therefore runs on the Mac, not on Netlify's servers, and consumes no\nNetlify build minutes. The marketing site is updated by dragging its folder onto\nthe Deploys tab.\n\nTwo Netlify sites, and they are easy to confuse. The app is\nreleve-app at app.relevestaffing.com; the marketing site is the other\none, at relevestaffing.com. Dragging the site folder onto the app by mistake\nreplaces the whole app with the static site, and because that folder's\n_redirects sends every path to index.html, even\n/api/jobs answers with the marketing homepage. It happened on\n3 September. The fix is simply to redeploy the app from Terminal. Check the\ndomain shown at the top of a site before dropping anything on it.\n\nSecrets\n\nAll in Netlify environment variables: the Supabase secret key, the SMTP app\npassword, the cron secret, and the Google client id and secret. Never in a file,\nnever with NEXT_PUBLIC_ in front.\n\nTwo single points of failure. The code exists on one Mac, and\nthe database has no backups. Both are free to fix and neither is done."
